            <ArticleTitle>Effects of OPC-8212, a new positive inotropic agent, and dobutamine on left ventricular global and ischemic regional functions and coronary hemodynamics under coronary artery stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>161-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have investigated the effects of OPC-8212, a new positive inotropic agent, and dobutamine, a known cardioselective inotropic agent, on global left ventricular (LV) and ischemic regional functions in 14 excised canine hearts with a flow-limiting stenosis of the left circumflex coronary artery (LCX) (i.e., 20-25% of control flow). OPC-8212 infusion (n = 7) under LCX stenosis improved cardiac depression [i.e., peak LV dP/dt increased from 1,295 +/- 143 mm Hg/s to 2,669 +/- 266 mm Hg/s (mean +/- SEM) (p less than 0.001)], while myocardial ischemic injury, assessed by myocardial CO2-tension and electrocardiogram (ECG)-ST changes, improved (i.e., delta CO2-tension and ECG-ST deviation decreased from 21.1 +/- 3.6 mm Hg and 3.8 +/- 0.6 mV to 13.3 +/- 2.8 mm Hg (p less than 0.01) and 2.0 +/- 0.7 mV (p less than 0.05), respectively). On the other hand, dobutamine infusion (n = 7) further increased myocardial CO2-tension and ECG-ST deviation [i.e., delta CO2-tension and ECG-ST deviation increased from 14.4 +/- 4.2 mm Hg and 2.5 +/- 1.2 mV to 29.0 +/- 6.0 mm Hg (p less than 0.01) and 4.9 +/- 1.0 mV (p less than 0.01), respectively]. At the same time, peak LV dP/dt clearly improved, but to a lesser degree; from 1,425 +/- 153 mm Hg/s to 2,393 +/- 245 mm Hg/s (p less than 0.001). There was also an increase in percent systolic segment shortening of each corresponding area as with OPC-8212.(ABSTRACT TRUNCATED AT 250 WORDS)</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
